[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GitoxideLabs/gitoxide/pulls/2530","id":3561235827,"node_id":"PR_kwDOCCL8X87URCVz","html_url":"https://github.com/GitoxideLabs/gitoxide/pull/2530","diff_url":"https://github.com/GitoxideLabs/gitoxide/pull/2530.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/GitoxideLabs/gitoxide/pull/2530.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GitoxideLabs/gitoxide/issues/2530","number":2530,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add reproductions for all known advisories","user":{"login":"Byron","id":63622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron","html_url":"https://github.com/Byron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Byron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Tasks\r\n\r\n* [x] commit and publish all tests\r\n* [x] refackview\r\n* [x] refackview fuzz\r\n* [x] fixes for remaining failing tests\r\n* [x] fuzz based failures\r\n    - [x] gix-pack\r\n    - [x] gix-index\r\n    - [x] wire up alloc_init_bytes to everything\r\n    - [x] enforce use of safe constructor (alloc_limit), it's plumbing and people should make a concious decision\r\n    - [x] alloc_limit default if repo is untrusted\r\n    - [x] Make sure the corpus seeds are picked up, corpus scripts exist - only used to avoid duplication\r\n    - [x] all other fuzz tests\r\n    - [x] scripts to produce corpus.zip for preseeded corpus\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nAdd a `gix-sec` reproducer showing that `is_path_owned_by_current_user()` trusts\r\na user-owned symlink instead of the symlink target, which can incorrectly mark\r\nnon-owned content as trusted.\r\n\r\nAdd a `gix-submodule` reproducer showing that a distributed `update = !command`\r\nfrom `.gitmodules` is accepted when a same-named local section exists, even if\r\nthat local section did not provide the winning `update` value.\r\n\r\nAdd a companion reproducer for the same provenance bug at the accessor layer,\r\nshowing that `File::update()` exposes a command that should remain forbidden\r\nwhen it originates from `.gitmodules`.\r\n\r\nAdd a `gix` repository-level reproducer showing that `open_modules_file()`\r\nand `submodules()` follow a worktree `.gitmodules` symlink and parse\r\nattacker-controlled bytes outside the repository.\r\n\r\nAdd a `gix` submodule reproducer for malicious submodule names with traversal\r\ncomponents, exercising `state()` and `open()` at the real API boundary used to\r\nderive and open submodule repositories.\r\n\r\nAdd a shared `gix` reproducer for submodule-name path traversal, covering\r\nrepository redirection outside `.git/modules` through the high-level submodule\r\nAPI.\r\n\r\nAdd a `gix-transport` HTTP reproducer for cross-host redirects, targeting\r\nthe curl backend and checking that redirected requests do not forward\r\n`Authorization` headers to the new host.\r\n\r\nAdd `gix-pack` reproducers for three denial-of-service vectors: malformed delta\r\ncopy instructions, truncated ref-delta metadata, and oversized declared result\r\nsizes that currently panic or overflow during pack decoding.\r\n","created_at":"2026-04-21T10:32:14Z","updated_at":"2026-08-16T17:22:17Z","closed_at":"2026-04-24T07:16:29Z","merged_at":"2026-04-24T07:16:29Z","merge_commit_sha":"63b841907ce30b36bb50da5aae3a9e1a06eadf64","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels